  "captions": [
    "Table A: Growth kinetic parameters of all eight strains at different storage temperatures in TSB and SJ, estimated from the primary model of Baranyi and Roberts (1994); maximum growth rate (max, logCFU/h), lag-phase duration (h), maximum population density (Ymax log CFU/g), R2 (the coefficient of determination), and SE (standard error of R2). Each sample point is represented as mean (n=3  SD). A two-way ANOVA and Tuckey post hoc were used to find significant differences on strain- and temperature level. Significant differences on strain level are illustrated with roman numeral (I/II/III), with corresponding p-values right below in the same column. Significant differences between the strains on each temperature are illustrated with letters (abc), and the corresponding p-values for each temperature are shown at the bottom of the table. NL: no lag, NG: no growth.",
    "Table B: Growth kinetic parameters of all eight strains in TSB at different concentrations of NaCl in combination with different storage temperatures, estimated from the primary model of Baranyi and Roberts (1994); maximum growth rate (max, logCFU/h), lag-phase duration (h), maximum population density (Ymax log CFU/g), R2 (the coefficient of determination), and SE (standard error of R2). Each sample point is represented as mean (n=3  SE). A two-way ANOVA and Tuckey post hoc were used to find significant differences on strain- and temperature level. Significant differences on strain level are illustrated with roman numeral (I/II/III), with corresponding p-values right below in the same column. Significant differences between the strains for each temperature are illustrated with letters (abc), and the corresponding p-values for each temperature are shown at the bottom of the table. NL: no lag, NG: no growth, NA: no asymptote.",
    "Table C: Growth kinetic parameters of all eight strains in TSB at different concentrations of PCS VTABB in combination with different storage temperatures, estimated from the primary model of Baranyi and Roberts (1994); maximum growth rate (max, logCFU/h), lag-phase duration (h), maximum population density (Ymax log CFU/g), R2 (the coefficient of determination), and SE (standard error of R2). Each sample point is represented as mean (n=3  SE). A two-way ANOVA and Tuckey post hoc were used to find significant differences on strain- and temperature level. Significant differences on strain level are illustrated with roman numeral (I/II/III), with corresponding p-values right below in the same column. Significant differences between the strains at each temperature are illustrated with letters (abc), and the corresponding p-values for each temperature are shown at the bottom of the table. NL: no lag, NG: no growth, NA: no asymptote. ",
    "Table D: Growth kinetic parameters of all eight strains in TSB at different concentrations of PCS JJT01 in combination with different storage temperatures, estimated from the primary model of Baranyi and Roberts (1994); maximum growth rate (max, logCFU/h), lag-phase duration (h), maximum population density (Ymax log CFU/g), R2 (the coefficient of determination), and SE (standard error of R2). Each sample point is represented as mean (n=3  SE). A two-way ANOVA and Tuckey post hoc were used to find significant differences on strain- and temperature level. Significant differences on strain level are illustrated with roman numeral (I/II/III), with corresponding p-values right below in the same column. Significant differences between the strains at each temperature are illustrated with letters (abc), and the corresponding p-values for each temperature are shown at the bottom of the table. NL: no lag, NG: no growth, NA: no asymptote."
  ],
